R&C patch 7066: the runtime's frameless host setjmp/longjmp on MinGW x64 no longer go through the CRT.

Issue #22 (Windows 10 19041, every run of ToD ended 0.6 s in): ucrtbase's longjmp calls __except_validate_jump_buffer
when Control Flow Guard is active in the process (Windows turns it on, Wine does not). It requires the buffer's Rsp to
lie in the thread's stack and its Frame to be non-zero, else __fastfail(13). The frameless form the runtime uses on
purpose (_setjmp(buf, NULL): KZ3 patch 1099 for the SPU halt/drain jumps, 1116 for the PPU guest setjmp host frames,
no RtlUnwindEx over lifted frames) writes Frame = 0, so the first such jump ended the process on Windows. Read from the
reporter's minidump: longjmp+0x14 -> __except_validate_jump_buffer+0x3c (`cmp qword [rdx], 0; jne; int 0x29`), the
buffer on the heap (the per-thread record table) with Frame = 0 and Rsp inside the stack.

runtime/platform/host_jmp_win64.h: rc_host_setjmp / rc_host_longjmp, naked ms_abi functions that save and restore the
Win64 callee-saved state (the same registers the CRT's frameless path restored), with no validation and no unwind.
ppu_setjmp.h (PPU_SJ_HOST_*), spu_context.h (SPU_SETJMP/SPU_LONGJMP), spu_channels.c and spu_drain.c use them on MinGW
x64 (each of the two .c files kept its own CRT longjmp before: a setjmp/longjmp pair from different layouts); other
hosts are unchanged. Host test: port/rc/tests/test_host_jmp_win64.c (built with GCC and clang, run under Wine).
Upstream candidate (affects every ps3recomp title built with MinGW on Windows).

